<title>UK: Kvaerner sells two properties for 443 NOK.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner sells two properties for 443 NOK.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian shipbuilding and engineering company Kvaerner Plc said it had signed agreements to sell two properties in Oslo for a total consideration of 443 million Norwegian crowns ($62.7 million).</p>
<p>The group said the disposals would provide it a profit of around 300 million crowns.  </p>
<p>The company said it was selling its Myrens Verksted property for 201 million crowns and another property at Skoyen for 242 million crowns.</p>
<p>Both transactions will be completed in May, 1997, it said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
